<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.1" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="42349-1" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Reason for referral (narrative)"/>
    <title>Reason for Referral</title>
    <text><paragraph>Suspected subungual melanoma of the right great toe in a 32-year-old musician and footballer with dark skin: a brown-black band about 5 mm wide that has not grown out in two months, with pigment on the proximal nail fold. A full-thickness nail matrix biopsy is booked with our dermatologist this week. Please see him with the result to advise on staging and definitive surgery. [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Urgency: Urgent, within two weeks, with the biopsy result. [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Questions for the consultant:</paragraph><list listType="ordered"><item>If the biopsy confirms melanoma, what is its stage, and what staging tests does he need?</item><item>Should he be offered a sentinel lymph node biopsy?</item><item>What are the surgical options, and is a digit-sparing operation safe for him, given what matters to him?</item><item>Will he need treatment after surgery, and how should he be followed?</item><item>How should he check his own skin and nails from now on?</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>He noticed the dark stripe about two months ago after a knock at football and was told at an urgent care clinic a month ago that it was a bruise. It has not grown out with the nail and the color has spread onto the skin at the base of the nail. The toe is barely sore. Examination: a brown-black longitudinal band about a third of the nail wide, with irregular dark lines, and pigment on the proximal nail fold (Hutchinson sign); the nail plate is intact; no nodule or ulcer; no popliteal or inguinal nodes. Fitzpatrick type VI skin. Otherwise well; no medicines; no known allergies; does not smoke tobacco. He tours as a musician, runs and plays football several times a week, and his Rastafari faith is central to how he makes decisions. He wants a clear explanation and time to decide about any treatment, and he decides who is told about his health [S]</paragraph><list><item>A dark stripe under the right big toenail that he put down to a knock at football about two months ago; it has not grown out, and the dark color has spread to the skin at the base of the nail. An urgent care clinician told him a month ago that it was a bruise. [S]</item><item>Wants a clear explanation and time to decide about any treatment; his faith, his music and his football all matter to him in that decision. [S]</item></list><paragraph>Historical basis. These claims are historical evidence, not findings from a modern examination.</paragraph><list><item>Robert Nesta Marley was born on February 6, 1945, at Nine Mile in Saint Ann Parish, Jamaica, the son of a Jamaican mother and a white English father. [D]</item><item>He was a Jamaican singer, songwriter and musician, considered one of the pioneers of reggae, who toured the world with his band, the Wailers. [D]</item><item>He was raised a Roman Catholic and converted to Rastafari in the late 1960s; he became known as a Rastafarian icon who infused his music with spirituality. [D]</item><item>In 1977 he noticed a pigmented lesion on the nail bed of his right great toe and thought it was the result of a football injury. The first physician he saw thought that a reasonable explanation; because the lesion was growing, he saw a second physician, who performed a biopsy. [D]</item><item>Whether the football injury caused the lesion is disputed: an encyclopedia article states that the lesion was not caused by the injury but was a sign of a cancer already present, and clinicians note that many people with acral melanoma recall an injury to the site, while the role of trauma is not established. [R]</item></list><paragraph>7 later historical claims are omitted because they describe events after the index age. See the teaching note.</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

