    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>A brown-black band in the right great toenail, about 5 mm wide (about a third of the nail), with irregular dark lines, first noticed about two months ago after a knock at football and not growing out with the nail; the pigment extends onto the skin of the proximal nail fold (Hutchinson sign). Suspected subungual melanoma; dermoscopy and a full-thickness nail matrix biopsy booked this week: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Dermoscopy of the nail and a full-thickness biopsy of the nail matrix at the origin of the band by the clinic&apos;s dermatologist within the week, with a full skin and nail examination including the palms and soles. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Melanoma: Cutaneous, Version 3.2026 (2026); Swetter SM, et al. Guidelines of care for the management of primary cutaneous melanoma. J Am Acad Dermatol 2019;80(1):208-250 (2019) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to surgical oncology, Naledi Mbeki-Rowe, MD, ordered 1977-06-08 [S]</item></list></text>

